From 3624328eaed49eba25b2ff129beb113ba86e645f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:26:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Touch controls: per-button drag-to-aim, fire modes and
 long-press lock, fire mode toggle

Lets one thumb attack/shove and aim while the other moves, without a
third finger. Everything is off by default and set in the touch editor.

Per key/mouse button (tap a button in the editor):
- Drag to aim: while a finger is held on the button, dragging it also
  moves the cursor like PAD mode (8 pt dead zone; speed slider in the
  editor panel appears once any button uses it).
- Long press to lock: a 0.5 s press keeps the button held after the
  finger lifts (gold ring + haptic), e.g. RC for hands-free aiming. The
  next tap, ESC, hiding the controls, or connecting a controller lets go.
  Only in the Default fire mode.
- Fire mode: Default (held while pressed), Auto (held and re-pressed
  every 0.25 s so the action repeats whatever the weapon) or Release
  (holding does nothing and shows amber, so you can aim without spamming;
  lifting the finger sends one press).

New "Fire mode toggle" control (Add menu): pick the button it changes
("Changes"); each tap in game cycles that button Default -> Auto ->
Release and shows the current mode (DEF/AUTO/REL) on the toggle.

